  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 218 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nThursday is pretty similar to Wednesday so we could have a repeat of \nshowers and storms if enough instability can be achieved and for \nthis have those low (~20%) pops in the forecast.  By Friday and into \nthe weekend the temperatures will increase, but precip chances will \ndecrease as the high gradually shifts to be more center over our \narea by Sunday.  So confidence is not high enough to make changes to \nour extended grids.  Will note that the high starts to very slowly \nbreak down Sunday and Monday, and that will bring those temperatures \nback into the 90s for the most part, with increased precipitation \nchances riding over the top of the ridge, which would be mainly the \nnorthern Panhandles.  \n\nWeber",
